+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"5922a1cd-8fc0-4483-950b-2980804e72d0","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The complex scenario has feature-auth changing `role` to 'superadmin' and feature-ui not changing `role` (keeping 'admin'). When merging feature-auth into main, main gets `{ role: 'superadmin', ... }`. Then merging feature-ui into main has:\n- base (feature-ui's base = state at fork): role='admin'\n- ours (main after feature-auth merge): role='superadmin'\n- theirs (feature-ui): role='admin' (unchanged from base)\n\nSo ours !== base, theirs === base → only we changed → take ours. No conflict on role.\n\nFor prefs:\n- base: { theme: 'light', lang: 'en' }\n- ours: { theme: 'light', lang: 'en' } (main didn't change prefs, was from feature-auth which also didn't change them)\n- theirs: { theme: 'dark', lang: 'fr' } \n\nSo ours === base → take theirs. No conflict.\n\nTo get a conflict, both branches must change the SAME field to different values. Let me have feature-ui also change the `role` field to something different than 'superadmin', or also change `flags.beta` back.","signature":"5922a1cd-8fc0-4483-950b-2980804e72d0"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":665,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":78848,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21efb348-5eed-4f03-b0c1-d524e18e7c9c","uuid":"9c950fe1-b3cd-4817-ad62-8756b85fb4ea"}
